 "title": "Hindi_Hate_Lexicon",
 "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/22031681",
 "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22031681",
 "description": "<p>This repository presents the Hindi Hate Lexicon, titled&nbsp; (HH-LEX<sub>21</sub>), comprising lexical items associated with targets of hate speech. Building on the original lexicon, (HH-LEX<sub>19</sub>), we identified 265 additional lexical terms specific to the HASOC Hindi 2021 dataset, which consists of 4594 tweets, to construct (HH-LEX<sub>21</sub>).&nbsp;The lexicon was developed through a comprehensive manual analysis of individual tweets. Each tweet was systematically examined to identify lexical terms that explicitly or implicitly indicate the target of hate speech. These terms primarily include proper nouns as well as descriptive references to the targeted entities.</p>\n<p>The lexicon is organised into three categories to facilitate systematic analysis: Explicit Target Groups (n=330), Implicit Targets (n=269), and Explicitly Targeted Personalities (n=428). Each category is further subdivided into relevant subcategories. In addition, a supplementary list of Hindi swear words (n=445) is compiled to support the study.</p>\n<p><em>In this version, the files are named according to their lexicon subcategories only. In Version v1.0, the file names contain more detailed information, including both the lexicon category and the corresponding subcategory.</em></p>\n<p>This lexicon dataset is of particular relevance to the NLP research community, especially researchers working on hate speech detection, Indic languages, non-English text, multilingual and low-resource settings, annotation studies, and model explainability.</p>\n<p>A detailed description of the lexicon is provided in the preprint linked in the Related Works section.</p>",
